      "text": "The publisher for *People We Meet on Vacation* is **Berkley**, and it was released in **2021**. It is generally considered a **standalone** novel, though it is by the same author as other romantic comedies and shares a similar tone/style with others in the genre.\n\nHere is a spoiler-free summary of the premise and structure based on the available information:\n\n**Premise:**\nThe novel centers on Poppy and Alex, two best friends who have maintained a close bond through an annual week-long vacation they take together for ten years. However, something happened two years ago that caused their friendship to implode, and now they haven't spoken. The book follows Poppy as she decides to reach out to Alex and plan one more trip to try and fix what broke between them.\n\n**Structure:**\nThe narrative makes significant use of a **dual timeline**. It alternates between the present, where Poppy and Alex are on this last-ditch vacation, and flashbacks to their previous trips and pivotal moments from the past ten years, which helps the reader piece together how their relationship evolved and eventually fell apart.",
